      "body": "Fixes #64497\n\n## Problem\n\nDP=2 × TP=2 on a 2-NUMA CPU host with explicit binds crashes `CPUWorker.__init__` with `IndexError`. DP rank 1 gets device ids `[2, 3]`, which `get_visible_memory_node()` reads as NUMA node ids. Neither exists on a 2-node host, so the filter returns an empty list and the `allowed_memory_nodes[0]` fallback (added for s390x in #40714) raises.\n\n`CpuPlatform.get_current_memory_usage()` reads the same ids, so DP rank 1 reports 0 bytes even when the crash is avoided.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`get_physical_gpu_ids_for_local_dp_rank()` gives each DP rank a block of `world_size` device ids. On CPU those are logical device indices, not NUMA node ids. #62867 started passing them to `get_visible_memory_node(assigned_node_ids)`, which filters the allowed NUMA node list by them. The filter is correct only when the ids happen to name existing NUMA nodes (e.g. DP=2 on a 4-node host). When they do not, the list is empty.\n\n## Fix\n\nFall back to the full allowed NUMA node list when the `assigned_node_ids` filter matches nothing. A partial overlap still narrows to the matching nodes, preserving #62867's DP NUMA affinity intent.\n\n## Duplicate check\n\nNo open PR addresses this. #62867 introduced the regression and is merged; this fixes the case it missed.\n\n## Testing\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/utils_/test_cpu_resource_utils.py -x\n# 20 passed\n```\n\nRed-green: reverting the `cpu_resource_utils.py` change makes `test_visible_memory_node_no_matching_id_falls_back_to_allowed` fail; restoring it turns all 20 green.\n\nTwo new tests cover the complete-miss fallback and the partial-match narrowing.\n\nThe issue's reproducer (DP=2 × TP=2 with explicit binds on a 2-NUMA host) needs a 2-NUMA CPU host and was not run locally; the unit tests exercise the exact filter that produces the empty list.\n\n## AI assistance\n\nAI assistance was used for investigation and code authoring. The change was reviewed line by line and the tests were run locally.\n",
